                <head>PE–31. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>A controversy arose in Peru over possession by the Texas Petroleum Company in
                    Peru of aerial photographs of Peru received from the United States Government
                    without clearance from the Peruvian Government. The problem was taken up by the
                    Peruvian Chamber of Deputies and publicized in the Peruvian press. The Peruvian
                    Government made representations to the American Embassy in Lima and fined the
                    company. Documentation on these developments is in Department of State file
                    723.022.</p>
            </div>
